Re-Cherry patch for XenosRecomp (Lollipop Chainsaw, 0x102A11xx containers).

Against hedge-dev/XenosRecomp 990d03b28a27b50277ee5d8d942e1c5f873869d1, the
pinned thirdparty/XenosRecomp submodule. The submodule is left checked out at
that commit WITH THIS PATCH APPLIED TO ITS WORKING TREE: the translator is built
from it, and tools/shaders/build_shader_cache.py passes the patched
thirdparty/XenosRecomp/XenosRecomp/shader_common.h to every translation. The
game build itself only uses smol-v, xxHash and zstd from the submodule.

  git -C thirdparty/XenosRecomp apply ../../tools/xenosrecomp/cherry.patch
  cmake -S thirdparty/XenosRecomp -B out/xenosrecomp -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++
  cmake --build out/xenosrecomp --target XenosRecomp

Regenerate after editing the tree:
  git -C thirdparty/XenosRecomp diff > tools/xenosrecomp/cherry.patch   (then re-add this header)

What it contains and why: docs/renderer/shaders.md. Generic fixes ported from
Kameo's kameo.patch; Kameo's v0x0E container adaptations are not.

